SUMMARY: 43 passed, 0 failed (run a077fe)

Note on the sign-up line: GoTrue rejects the reserved .test domain (400 email_address_invalid, mapped to 422), so that probe
did NOT exercise the e-mail path. A second probe through the public route with agos-r204-probe2@example.com (06:48:21 UTC)
returned 429 "too many attempts; retry later"; Supabase auth log for that request:
  path=/signup status=429 error_code=over_email_send_rate_limit "email rate limit exceeded" (actor_username agos-r204-probe2@example.com)
  -> no user row remained (auth.users count for that address = 0).
Meaning: sign-up works up to the e-mail step, but with the built-in Supabase mailer (2 e-mails/hour, and Supabase only
delivers built-in mail to the project's team addresses) real users cannot reliably receive the confirmation e-mail.
Custom SMTP is an OWNER decision (provider/account/cost) — NOT done, and autoconfirm stays OFF on purpose.

