## 11. Not done / open (honest list)
  - 003 is not yet applied live (after merge; recorded in the acceptance log).
  - real-user sign-up e-mail delivery: needs custom SMTP (owner decision, §7).
  - Google/GitHub OAuth: client apps are the owner's (callback https://qehloiuyzksnijstkfmn.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback); providers stay disabled.
  - logout ends the Supabase session (verified: the old access token is 401 immediately because every policy checks
    session_is_active()). A token of a still-active session lives up to jwt_exp=3600 s; shortening it is optional (owner).
  - not measured: the per-IP limiter key behind the Render proxy (uvicorn trusts X-Forwarded-For only from 127.0.0.1 by
    default, so request.client.host may be the proxy address — clients could share one bucket). Pre-existing v1 behaviour
    shared by /api/v2; recorded as an open question, not changed in R-204.
